15
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,620
No way.

16
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:49,780
If that's true, that would make your regenerative powers greater than my own.

17
00:02:49,780 --> 00:03:19,760
I'll see you next time.

18
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:21,680
She'll never be the same.

19
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:35,200
Get off me, you damn brat!

20
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:45,460
I'll chop you into pieces and stuff you into my belt!

21
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:56,840
She stopped it with her severed limbs?

22
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:59,020
No.

23
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:01,900
Her coagulated blood is keeping them connected.

24
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,840
Her blood is burning me!

25
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,560
Just like that day!

26
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:14,820
Fire!

27
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,040
Fire!

28
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:16,120
Fire!

29
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:21,820
Fire!

30
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:33,320
Fire!

31
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,460
Fire!

32
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:39,040
Here we go.

33
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:34,440
Oh, my God.

34
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:59,100
No, don't. You have to stop it.

35
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:03,680
Listen to me. You can pull through this.

36
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:12,660
Please forgive me. It's my fault you had to fight.

37
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:17,660
This whole area reeks of Nezuko's blood now.

38
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:22,140
I can tell just how badly she was wounded during the time I was passed out.

39
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:32,000
It hurt you, didn't it? I know you suffered. I'm sorry, but it's all right now. I promise I won't let anyone hurt you ever again.

40
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:36,620
You've got to go to sleep, Nezuko. Go to sleep so you can heal yourself.

41
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:39,380
Nezuko!

42
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:41,740
Please.

43
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:49,300
What's going on?

44
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,460
I don't know. They just burst through the floors.

45
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:56,180
Zu... come. Just sleep.

46
00:06:56,180 --> 00:07:04,540
You've got some nerve doing that to me.

47
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:08,920
So, you can use blood demon art as well.

48
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:12,820
I've never heard of a blood demon art that only burns demons.

49
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:16,520
Whatever you did is taking me forever to heal from.

50
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:19,620
You're starting to irritate me like no other.

51
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,420
I'm through playing around.

52
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,560
This is bad.

53
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:26,100
There are people here that I have to protect.

54
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,040
I have to think and take action.

55
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:33,860
Her attack will come any second now, which will shred this whole building.

56
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,760
I can't just let go of Nezuko.

57
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:40,980
But if I don't, these people will get hurt.

58
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:54,820
Hey.

59
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,800
So, is this Nezuko Kamado?

60
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:01,200
Quite the flashy way to demonize.

61
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:04,500
When did you get here?

62
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:08,320
All that fancy talk in front of the Master?

63
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,380
And you let her wreak havoc like this?

64
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:12,900
No one said she could demonize so flashily!

65
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:15,880
Thanks for coming.

66
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,800
You're a Hashira, right?

67
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:20,320
I've been here waiting for you.

68
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:22,100
Shut up.

69
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,080
I'm not here to waste my time on you.

70
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,060
Get lost.

71
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,880
After all, you're no upper-ranked demon.

72
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,640
Not when you're that weak.

73
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:33,260
You're not the one I've been searching for.

74
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:34,340
So beat it.

75
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:36,480
Come again?

76
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,540
How dare you speak to...

77
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:45,740
Huh?

78
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:57,740
Damn it!

79
00:08:58,700 --> 00:08:59,200
Damn it!

80
00:08:59,280 --> 00:08:59,800
Damn it!

81
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:03,080
How did we lose sight of the God of Festivals already?

82
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,580
At this rate, we'll be locked in the dark!

83
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,840
In a flashy way, of course.

84
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:19,740
Hey, you spotted him?

85
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:23,340
I hope you're ready, worm lady!

86
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,480
Cause the mountain god lordy knows how you're coming through!

87
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:34,480
Wait...

88
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,400
What?

89
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:38,680
She's beheaded!

90
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:40,680
But how?

91
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,980
Was it Mr. Uzui who did that?

92
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:44,820
He's unreal!

93
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:46,540
Hey!

94
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,240
The battle here is far from over.

95
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,340
So get her under control.

96
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:54,140
Yes, I'll go!

97
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:02,500
Brats who throw temper tantrums don't belong on the battlefield.

98
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,780
Can't you sing her a lullaby or something?

99
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:26,420
It's no use.

100
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,300
My voice isn't reaching her.

101
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:30,800
She's not listening to me at all.

102
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:33,740
Mother...

103
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:35,100
What do I do?

104
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:40,980
Can't you sing her a lullaby or something?

105
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:46,640
Hush, hush, baby rabbit!

106
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,860
Up there on the hill!

107
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:51,400
Why are your...

108
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,880
Ears so very long!

109
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,280
When I was small!

110
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:57,260
Mother!

111
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:57,380
Mother!

112
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:05,460
Eat...

113
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:07,160
The leaves...

114
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,400
Of a tall tree!

115
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,000
And that's why...

116
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,200
My...

117
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,120
Ears...

118
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,660
Are so long!

119
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:28,400
Nesuko?

120
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:32,400
Nesuko?

121
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:36,000
Nesuko?

122
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:43,240
Hush, baby rabbit!

123
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,240
Baby rabbit!

124
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:48,180
Up there on the hill!

125
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:53,620
Why is it your eyes are so red, my little rabbit?

126
00:11:53,620 --> 00:12:06,860
You see, before I was ever born, my mother decided one day to eat the red fruit of the tree.

127
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:13,820
So little bunny that I might be, my eyes are red from that tree.

128
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:19,760
I think I'm starting to get what happened now.

129
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:25,240
So the reason brother's eyes are red, is because you ate red berries when he was inside your tummy.

130
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:50,240
Nesuko?

131
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:50,920
Nesuko?

132
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,920
Nesuko?

133
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,920
Nesuko?

134
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:56,920
Nesuko?

135
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:57,920
Nesuko?

136
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,920
Nesuko?

137
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,920
Nesuko?

138
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:18,920
Nesuko?

139
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,920
It worked.

140
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,920
You hear that, Mother?

141
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:25,000
That mother, it worked. She's sound asleep.

142
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,000
Mr. Uzui...

143
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:32,000
Where do you think you're going? Get back here, you brute!

144
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:36,460
You have the gall to behead me and walk away? You're going to pay for this!

145
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:43,580
Would you just shut up already? You've been nothing but unflashy, so drop dead.

146
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:49,920
Don't give me that crap! I'm stronger than you! So what makes you think that I'm not an upper rank?

147
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,500
Sorry, but you can't be an upper rank.

148
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,880
I will have you know that I am upper six!

149
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:58,740
Then why are you holding your severed head right now? I mean, come on.

150
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:00,620
What, did I cut your brains out too?

151
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:05,420
Just because I'm like this doesn't mean I've lost yet! I'm an upper rank, dammit!

152
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,580
I think it's pretty obvious that you lost.

153
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:14,840
I'm just more powerful than you can comprehend! I might be number six right now, but I'm going to get even stronger!

154
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,660
Don't care, didn't ask.

155
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:30,140
I really have an upper six! I really have an upper six! I've even got the number to prove it too!

156
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,760
You just can't accept how amazing I am!

157
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,100
You're kidding. She's throwing a tantrum?

158
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,340
Wait a second. How is she able to talk for this long?

159
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:42,380
Even though she was beheaded, her body hasn't disintegrated.

160
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:46,500
Die! Die! Die! All of you can just die!

161
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:56,880
He cut my head off! He cut my head off!

162
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:59,580
Help me, brother!

163
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:24,840
Come on now. There's no use crying about it, you know?

164
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:29,540
Can't you even manage to reattach your own head by yourself?

165
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:34,140
Well, you haven't always been the sharpest tool in the shed, have you?

166
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,340
She's still alive even after I beheaded her.

167
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:40,240
More importantly, who's that guy with her?

168
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,900
His reflexes are unreal.

169
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:46,100
Oh, is that a burn on your face?

170
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:50,240
You need to learn how to take better care of your face, you know?

171
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:55,380
After all, you were born with such a pretty face compared to mine.

172
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:07,280
Oh, not bad. I was going in for the kill, you know.

173
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:11,740
But you were able to stop me, weren't you?

174
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,440
Good for you.

175
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:14,780
Really.

176
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:19,160
You're a lucky guy, aren't you?

177
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,700
That face of yours.

178
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:24,600
Nice. I like your skin, too.

179
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:28,940
Not a blemish birthmark or scar to be seen anywhere, huh?

180
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,900
And you've got some meat on your bones.

181
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,380
I can't gain weight no matter what, see?

182
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:37,600
And you're tall as well.

183
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:41,060
You look like you're well over six feet, aren't you?

184
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:46,560
I guess you must get tons of attention from the ladies, don't you?

185
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:49,200
I envy you.

186
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,400
Oh, I envy you.

187
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:57,240
Would you mind just dropping dead and in the most agonizing way at the end?

188
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:01,840
Like getting skinned alive or maybe even getting that belly of yours lit open?

189
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:05,020
And one more thing, you oversized meat sack.

190
00:17:05,380 --> 00:17:06,280
Brother, wait.

191
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:09,000
He's not the only one who was arresting me.

192
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,240
Kill the ones who burned me, too.

193
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,140
Kill them.

194
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:15,060
I've been toiling away over here and yet...

195
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:18,680
Even though I've given it my all, they won't die!

196
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:23,360
I feel like they tried everything, but they kept getting back up and picking on me!

197
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:27,120
They kicked up and bullied me, and I can't take it anymore!

198
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:32,780
I think I understand what's happening now, and what you did to her was unforgivable!

199
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:39,320
My sweet little sister was doing her best with what little brain she had to work with, and you bullied her!

200
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:43,720
I'll have to massacre everyone who laid a finger on her.

201
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:47,340
You could say I'm a firm believer in vengeance.

202
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:51,420
So I'll exact the same pain you inflicted upon her.

203
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:55,020
When you die, those words will ring through your skull.

204
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:58,980
I'll show no mercy, because my name is Gyataro!

205
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,060
What are those?

206
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:08,240
Sickles?

207
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,340
They're heading back towards Mr. Uzui.

208
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,540
Something's not right.

209
00:18:15,060 --> 00:18:16,960
The belt demon never used a sickle.

210
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:18,700
Is it a new demon?

211
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:21,000
I smell Mr. Uzui's blood.

212
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:22,520
I've gotta back him up!

213
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:25,660
Where are you, worm belt?

214
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:28,020
Lord Inosuke has arrived!

215
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:30,180
You can run, but you can't hide!

216
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,160
Inosuke, Zenitsu...

217
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:34,660
Zenitsu, are you asleep?

218
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,780
You two, go and help Mr. Uzui.

219
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,440
Hurry!

220
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,940
Sit back, relax, and leave it to me!

221
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,780
I'm ready to go for a snack!

222
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:47,080
Yours truly, Lord Inosuke will handle it!

223
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,660
Hey, flash in me!

224
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,120
Thanks.

225
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:52,420
I'll put Nezuko back in her box.

226
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:54,360
It should only take a second!

227
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,540
I will allow it!

228
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:56,260
Thank you!

229
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:05,220
I'm so envious I could die.

230
00:19:05,880 --> 00:19:08,960
You really are a good-looking guy, aren't you?

231
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:09,780
Damn!

232
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:13,020
Protecting those humans?

233
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,080
Showing off like that?

234
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:17,280
I envy you.

235
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:22,660
In their eyes, you're some kind of brave hero, aren't you?

236
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:28,620
I bet their affection and gratitude towards you is immeasurable, you know?

237
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,280
Well, yeah.

238
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:34,000
I'm a flashy, glamorous ladies' man, so that's a no-brainer.

239
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,920
Not to brag, but I have three wives to boot.

240
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:43,020
Am I going deaf, or did you just say that you have three wives?

241
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,120
You've gotta be kidding me!

242
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:48,240
That's unforgivable!

243
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:48,320
That's unforgivable!

244
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,340
Blood demon art!

245
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:55,540
Flying blood sickle!

246
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:59,700
These splashes of blood are like blades.

247
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:00,880
It's so many of them!

248
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,780
I have to protect the people.

249
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:07,700
What now?

250
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:08,700
An explosion?

251
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:11,400
So you're on the first floor now.

252
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:12,460
Run!

253
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:13,480
Quickly!

254
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:18,140
Like I've let you escape that easily.

255
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,900
Bend for me, flying blood sickles.

256
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:30,360
He can control each of the slashes.

257
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:33,360
Which means he'll keep moving them until they hit their target.

258
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,900
The sister didn't die even when she was decapitated.

259
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:38,240
That's unheard of.

260
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:40,120
Since these two are siblings,

261
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:43,440
can I get rid of them both if I behead the brother instead?

262
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,780
Is he the main unit?

263
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:50,420
One way to find out.

264
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,540
From what I can hear,

265
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,480
all the people upstairs have fled.

266
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:04,240
